{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks","id":1470706,"title":"Celerity and surprise attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-17T05:56:17-08:00","id":1470706,"title":"Celerity and surprise attacks","content":"The manual states that the active effect of celerity that lets you multiply your speed by your dots of celerity plus one allows you to lunch surprise attacks, how would this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T06:33:53-08:00","id":1470707,"title":"","content":"It would allow you to use the rules for Surprise on page 176.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T06:43:38-08:00","id":1470708,"title":"","content":"Even in combat? this question came up in my last game and nobody knew the answer, the situation was that a player used celerity to interrupt an hunter and get behind him, he asked the ST if he should have rolled for a surprise attack and the ST admitted that he had no idea, this would be a game changer for a lot of combat related encounters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T09:44:06-08:00","id":1470716,"title":"","content":"This same question come up long time ago. Rule are not clear at all. <br /> It may seem a bit OP if you can use in combat as many time you want but, as it's written, would lead me to interpret like this. There is no limitation of usage as for interrupt. <br /> Stating that it's only applicable outside combat for me doesn't have much sense. Outside combat you may be able to lunch Surprise attacks anyway. <br /> We personally do not use this part but I wouldn't argue if someone stated it should be possibile to use in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T09:58:01-08:00","id":1470717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470716#post1470716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This same question come up long time ago. Rule are not clear at all.<br /> It may seem a bit OP if you can use in combat as many time you want but, as it's written, would lead me to interpret like this. There is no limitation of usage as for interrupt.<br /> Stating that it's only applicable outside combat for me doesn't have much sense. Outside combat you may be able to lunch Surprise attacks anyway.<br /> We personally do not use this part but I wouldn't argue if someone stated it should be possibile to use in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically interrupt can be used only for as many dots of celerity you have per scene, it does seem a bit OP but frankly, thats the whole schtick of celerity, in my particular case the ST ruled that the PC could have attacked only factoring half of the defence of the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T10:04:20-08:00","id":1470719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470717#post1470717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Technically interrupt can be used only for as many dots of celerity you have per scene, it does seem a bit OP but frankly, thats the whole schtick of celerity, in my particular case the ST ruled that the PC could have attacked only factoring half of the defence of the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surprise is not tied to interrupt but to the speee multiplier which has no limit per scene. <br /> It is OP if you can neglet, every turn, defense to your opponent with only 1 bp. But, as I said, there are even more OP discipline, like dominate (yes even in combat as it requires one turn and 0 vitae to calm down the target).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T10:12:32-08:00","id":1470720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470719#post1470719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surprise is not tied to interrupt but to the speee multiplier which has no limit per scene.<br /> It is OP if you can neglet, every turn, defense to your opponent with only 1 bp. But, as I said, there are even more OP discipline, like dominate (yes even in combat as it requires one turn and 0 vitae to calm down the target).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly it would kinda make sense, you are basically flash stepping behind your opponent so he definitelly shouldn't be able to defend himself without an ambush check, besides, like you arleady said, there are even more OP disciplines in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T12:03:49-08:00","id":1470725,"title":"","content":"The rules for <i>surprise</i> are clear as glass: Anyone who is surprised can't take instant actions or apply their Defense during the <b>first turn of combat</b>. Using Celerity to facilitate surprise attacks means you get to initiate combat as if it was an ambush without having to hide or do any other actions to try to surprise your opponent. Also, nothing says you leave out the roll to notice surprise attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T13:43:00-08:00","id":1470737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470725#post1470725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for <i>surprise</i> are clear as glass: Anyone who is surprised can't take instant actions or apply their Defense during the <b>first turn of combat</b>. Using Celerity to facilitate surprise attacks means you get to initiate combat as if it was an ambush without having to hide or do any other actions to try to surprise your opponent. Also, nothing says you leave out the roll to notice surprise attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get starting combat with an ambush but what I meant was during actual combat, after the first round, could a vampire spam as many ambush attacks as he has blood? like costantly moving around to attack his opponent from behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T13:46:40-08:00","id":1470738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470737#post1470737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get starting combat with an ambush but what I meant was during actual combat, after the first round, could a vampire spam as many ambush attacks as he has blood? like costantly moving around to attack his opponent from behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the rules, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T13:54:33-08:00","id":1470739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470738#post1470738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the rules, no.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What rule says so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:13:26-08:00","id":1470741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470739#post1470739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rule says so?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule that states that surprise attacks only occur during the first turn of combat. Just because that specific effect of Celerity can be used during combat doesn't mean you can ignore the qualifying part of the surprise rules. Note that Celerity says that you &quot;may&quot; use the effect to launch surprise attacks. That doesn't mean you're automatically granted the opportunity to make a surprise attack regardless of other circumstances. You wouldn't assume you could just re-hide with a successful Stealth roll during combat to launch a new surprise attack despite it not being the first turn of combat, so why would you think Celerity would allow you to do that?<br /> You could absolutely devise a new rule to handle unexpected attacks during combat (a rule that is unfortunately missing from the game), and it would be rational to model it on the existing rules of surprise, but that would be a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:44:17-08:00","id":1470744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470741#post1470741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rule that states that surprise attacks only occur during the first turn of combat. Just because that specific effect of Celerity can be used during combat doesn't mean you can ignore the qualifying part of the surprise rules. Note that Celerity says that you &quot;may&quot; use the effect to launch surprise attacks. That doesn't mean you're automatically granted the opportunity to make a surprise attack regardless of other circumstances. You wouldn't assume you could just re-hide with a successful Stealth roll during combat to launch a new surprise attack despite it not being the first turn of combat, so why would you think Celerity would allow you to do that?<br /> You could absolutely devise a new rule to handle unexpected attacks during combat (a rule that is unfortunately missing from the game), and it would be rational to model it on the existing rules of surprise, but that would be a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way the rule is worded, it doesn't outright say that you can only surprise someone in the first turn, also hiding again with stealth might be far fetched but using a discipline like obfuscate would technically allow you to disappear while in combat so how is celerity different? to your opponent you would look like you are teleporting around it and there would be no way he would be capable of realizing you are going to attack until it is too late, I'm fine either way since celerity is plenty powerful already but I find the idea of being able to flash step behind people to be really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:57:59-08:00","id":1470746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470744#post1470744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the rule is worded, it doesn't outright say that you can only surprise someone in the first turn, also hiding again with stealth might be far fetched but using a discipline like obfuscate would technically allow you to disappear while in combat so how is celerity different? to your opponent you would look like you are teleporting around it and there would be no way he would be capable of realizing you are going to attack until it is too late, I'm fine either way since celerity is plenty powerful already but I find the idea of being able to flash step behind people to be really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 176, &quot;Surprise&quot;:<br /> &quot;Any character who fails the roll cannot take an action <b>in the first turn of combat</b>, and can\u2019t apply Defense <b>for that turn</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also think that's a pretty cool idea. That's why we've homebrewed Quicker Than Sight:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Quicker than Sight</b></i><br /> <i>(Celerity \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> This relatively rare Devotion is based on the idea that an enemy cannot defend against what they cannot see coming. While most Kindred would let such subtleties go through the Obfuscate Discipline, some few have chosen speed rather than deception. Quicker than sight is a trick that allows the Vampire to strike before anyone watching them could possibly have reacted, to most the vampire is simply a momentary blur, and their enemy falls down dead. This Devotion is rarely taught from one Kindred to another, but rather individually developed when Kindred have contemplated the value of speed. Versions of this power have been developed by Kindred as far apart as Japan and the American Southwest.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> When activated, Quicker than Sight lasts for a single attack, but that attack is so fast that unless the Vampire\u2019s victim has any defense that applies against firearms, they simply cannot react quick enough to apply defense.<br /> This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to learn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> It requires a little more investment, and is naturally countered by anything which grants Defense vs firearms (such as Celerity, partially, and the Quicken Sight Devotion from the core book). It's actually even more powerful than your interpretation of base Celerity since it bypasses the surprise roll completely, so it might not be to your liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T14:58:26-08:00","id":1470747,"title":"","content":"Just grab/make a cheap Merit or Devotion that explicitly allows mid-battle reestablishment of Surprise, because by current RAW no one can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T15:02:59-08:00","id":1470748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470746#post1470746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 176, &quot;Surprise&quot;:<br /> &quot;Any character who fails the roll cannot take an action <b>in the first turn of combat</b>, and can\u2019t apply Defense <b>for that turn</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also think that's a pretty cool idea. That's why we've homebrewed Quicker Than Sight:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Quicker than Sight</b></i><br /> <i>(Celerity \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> This relatively rare Devotion is based on the idea that an enemy cannot defend against what they cannot see coming. While most Kindred would let such subtleties go through the Obfuscate Discipline, some few have chosen speed rather than deception. Quicker than sight is a trick that allows the Vampire to strike before anyone watching them could possibly have reacted, to most the vampire is simply a momentary blur, and their enemy falls down dead. This Devotion is rarely taught from one Kindred to another, but rather individually developed when Kindred have contemplated the value of speed. Versions of this power have been developed by Kindred as far apart as Japan and the American Southwest.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> When activated, Quicker than Sight lasts for a single attack, but that attack is so fast that unless the Vampire\u2019s victim has any defense that applies against firearms, they simply cannot react quick enough to apply defense.<br /> This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to learn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> It requires a little more investment, and is naturally countered by anything which grants Defense vs firearms (such as Celerity, partially, and the Quicken Sight Devotion from the core book). It's actually even more powerful than your interpretation of base Celerity since it bypasses the surprise roll completely, so it might not be to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this devotion, I'm going to ask my ST if he can add it, still its a shame that the writers didn't thought about such a possibility for celerity, I'm alway uncomfortable whenever I have to use an homebrew rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T15:47:48-08:00","id":1470749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470746#post1470746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 176, &amp;quot;Surprise&amp;quot;:<br /> &amp;quot;Any character who fails the roll cannot take an action <b>in the first turn of combat</b>, and can\u2019t apply Defense <b>for that turn</b>.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I also think that's a pretty cool idea. That's why we've homebrewed Quicker Than Sight:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i><b>Quicker than Sight</b></i><br /> <i>(Celerity \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> This relatively rare Devotion is based on the idea that an enemy cannot defend against what they cannot see coming. While most Kindred would let such subtleties go through the Obfuscate Discipline, some few have chosen speed rather than deception. Quicker than sight is a trick that allows the Vampire to strike before anyone watching them could possibly have reacted, to most the vampire is simply a momentary blur, and their enemy falls down dead. This Devotion is rarely taught from one Kindred to another, but rather individually developed when Kindred have contemplated the value of speed. Versions of this power have been developed by Kindred as far apart as Japan and the American Southwest.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> When activated, Quicker than Sight lasts for a single attack, but that attack is so fast that unless the Vampire\u2019s victim has any defense that applies against firearms, they simply cannot react quick enough to apply defense.<br /> This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to learn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> It requires a little more investment, and is naturally countered by anything which grants Defense vs firearms (such as Celerity, partially, and the Quicken Sight Devotion from the core book). It's actually even more powerful than your interpretation of base Celerity since it bypasses the surprise roll completely, so it might not be to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says: &quot;cannot take actions the first turn of a combat&quot; cause after the surprise attack happens your enemy is able to react during the following turns. It doesn't mean you can't re-establish surprise. Obfuscate 3 is, for example, able to re-establish surprise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T15:59:30-08:00","id":1470750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470749#post1470749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says: &quot;cannot take actions the first turn of a combat&quot; cause after the surprise attack happens your enemy is able to react during the following turns. It doesn't mean you can't re-establish surprise. Obfuscate 3 is, for example, able to re-establish surprise...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats what I was thinking, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T16:00:36-08:00","id":1470751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470749#post1470749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says: &quot;cannot take actions the first turn of a combat&quot; cause after the surprise attack happens your enemy is able to react during the following turns. It doesn't mean you can't re-establish surprise. Obfuscate 3 is, for example, able to re-establish surprise...</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither the surprise rules nor Obfuscate 3 say this. Obfuscate 3 says that it adds your Obfuscate dots to the surprise roll if you attack somebody.<br /> <br /> Combat starts with all sides' players declaring intent, Initiative is rolled, and the contested roll between a character launching a surprise attack and their target is checked to see if it applies during the first turn of combat.<br /> <br /> After that first turn, being unable to see an attack coming is handled by Defense only applying to attacks you're aware of, which is handled with the same basic roll for establishing surprise because it uses the same Traits.<br /> <br /> If you want to deny a target another turn, you apply Tilts like Stunned that do that or you retreat and make another ambush later in the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T16:28:09-08:00","id":1470752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470751#post1470751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither the surprise rules nor Obfuscate 3 say this. Obfuscate 3 says that it adds your Obfuscate dots to the surprise roll if you attack somebody.<br /> <br /> Combat starts with all sides' players declaring intent, Initiative is rolled, and the contested roll between a character launching a surprise attack and their target is checked to see if it applies during the first turn of combat.<br /> <br /> After that first turn, being unable to see an attack coming is handled by Defense only applying to attacks you're aware of, which is handled with the same basic roll for establishing surprise because it uses the same Traits.<br /> <br /> If you want to deny a target another turn, you apply Tilts like Stunned that do that or you retreat and make another ambush later in the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 3, Surprise Attack then you enter in combat, your next action you use obfuscate 3, if enemy either attack you and miss or already attacked you before your action, you then have the chance to do another Surprise Attack within the same combat. You can see that as getting out to the first combat to enter in another combat, but this doesn't change the fact you may be able to perform more than one Surprise in the same scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T02:55:53-08:00","id":1470774,"title":"","content":"Where in the description for Obfuscate 3 does it say that you can re-establish surprise?<br /> All I can see is that if you use Obfuscate 3 when attacking someone who can't see you, you get to add your Obfuscate dots to the surprise roll. I don't see where it says that you can do the surprise roll even though you're no longer qualified to use the surprise rules.<br /> <br /> Just because Obfuscate grants a bonus to a certain roll doesn't mean you get to roll that if other rules doesn't allow for it to be rolled. And even if you did get to roll surprise, you wouldn't gain any benefits whatsoever because surprise only affects characters during the first turn of combat. That's a core part of the surprise rules.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason Celerity can't be used to gain surprise during combat: The fact that System A gives a benefit to System B doesn't mean you can use System A to invoke System B outside the stated limits for System B. Not without System A explicitly changing that limit, which it doesn't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T03:40:17-08:00","id":1470775,"title":"","content":"One of the activated effects of Vigor allows you to lift and throw large objects. Would you say that you could use Vigor to lift and throw stuff around even if your arms are tied? If they're broken or outright missing? If there's nothing around to lift or throw?<br /> Using Vigor to boost your lifting and throwing capabilities doesn't mean in any way, shape, or form that you're automatically able to lift and throw stuff if other circumstances makes it impossible.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with using Celerity or Obfuscate to make surprise attacks during combat: The rules for surprise attacks doesn't work during combat so you can't make surprise attacks during combat regardless of how much Celerity or Obfuscate would boost surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> It's a shame there's a glaring hole in the combat rules for unexpected attacks outside the very first turn of combat, and in my games there would be no questions about unexpected attacks ignoring Defense (the victim would still retain their attack since they're already aware of them being in combat, and unless the attack is nondetectable (which is generally terrible game design so almost certainly not) a roll would still be made to see if the attack actually is unexpected) but that's a clear example of a houserule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T04:31:00-08:00","id":1470777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470775#post1470775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the activated effects of Vigor allows you to lift and throw large objects. Would you say that you could use Vigor to lift and throw stuff around even if your arms are tied? If they're broken or outright missing? If there's nothing around to lift or throw?<br /> Using Vigor to boost your lifting and throwing capabilities doesn't mean in any way, shape, or form that you're automatically able to lift and throw stuff if other circumstances makes it impossible.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with using Celerity or Obfuscate to make surprise attacks during combat: The rules for surprise attacks doesn't work during combat so you can't make surprise attacks during combat regardless of how much Celerity or Obfuscate would boost surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> It's a shame there's a glaring hole in the combat rules for unexpected attacks outside the very first turn of combat, and in my games there would be no questions about unexpected attacks ignoring Defense (the victim would still retain their attack since they're already aware of them being in combat, and unless the attack is nondetectable (which is generally terrible game design so almost certainly not) a roll would still be made to see if the attack actually is unexpected) but that's a clear example of a houserule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that my current ST had a good idea regarding sneak attack with celerity, he simply rulled that any attack carried this way carries a malus of current celerity+1 to the defence pool of the opponent for the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T06:29:23-08:00","id":1470780,"title":"","content":"The rules are pretty clear about no surprise attack being possible after combat starts, and since surprise affects action economy, it makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> also already said that unexpected attacks already ignore Defense, there's just no direct rule for that, which isn't so much of a problem.<br /> <br /> Making your attack be unexpected is far more complex than just being fast. The way Celerity handles things I'm already disinclined to think it naturally allows that amount of speed. You may be fast, but your opponent is already aware of a combat going on, reacting to you as best as possible, and a turn is just too short an amount of time anyway to change that expectation. You're fast, but not a bullet.<br /> <br /> Now, Merits and Devotions to solve that are another thing, while personally I wouldn't handle that just with speed. Blinking behind of your opponent doesn't change that your opponent is in the high-adrenaline state of a fight and expecting things from any direction, especially if they know how fast you are. Feinting and otherwise fooling your opponent makes a lot more sense to handle this, and should take into account their ability to see through your trick.<br /> <br /> But personally I'm against even firearms having this silly benefit of ignoring Defense. A person may be unable to dodge a bullet, but it is still far harder to correctly <i>aim</i> at a target actively avoiding to be aimed at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T06:50:43-08:00","id":1470781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470780#post1470780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules are pretty clear about no surprise attack being possible after combat starts, and since surprise affects action economy, it makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> also already said that unexpected attacks already ignore Defense, there's just no direct rule for that, which isn't so much of a problem.<br /> <br /> Making your attack be unexpected is far more complex than just being fast. The way Celerity handles things I'm already disinclined to think it naturally allows that amount of speed. You may be fast, but your opponent is already aware of a combat going on, reacting to you as best as possible, and a turn is just too short an amount of time anyway to change that expectation. You're fast, but not a bullet.<br /> <br /> Now, Merits and Devotions to solve that are another thing, while personally I wouldn't handle that just with speed. Blinking behind of your opponent doesn't change that your opponent is in the high-adrenaline state of a fight and expecting things from any direction, especially if they know how fast you are. Feinting and otherwise fooling your opponent makes a lot more sense to handle this, and should take into account their ability to see through your trick.<br /> <br /> But personally I'm against even firearms having this silly benefit of ignoring Defense. A person may be unable to dodge a bullet, but it is still far harder to correctly <i>aim</i> at a target actively avoiding to be aimed at.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are severely underestimating the amount of speed celerity grant &quot;The vampire appears to shift from point to point without crossing the space in-between&quot; it might not be a bullet but its definitely not something that you can easily predict and fight against, especially if you suddenly shift behind an opponent, a further penalty to his defence would be the minimum IMO.<br /> <br /> I absolutely agree on firearms ignoring defense being stupid, shooting a moving target is a considerably difficult thing even at close range, I think that V5 handled it better here by allowing to use your defense to simulate running for cover and making firearms much more lethal to justify their use over melee weapons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-18-2021, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T07:23:23-08:00","id":1470783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470781#post1470781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are severely underestimating the ammount of speed celerity grant</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I just disagree that this speed equates to a penalty on Defense.<br /> <br /> Celerity has still a key limitation: you're still having only one action a turn. It gives you a burst of speed, but not an equal burst of <i>perception</i>. Your reaction time is, indeed, improved, but not by that much.<br /> <br /> It is the exact same situation of the bullet. Your target can't react properly, which is already covered by <i>Interrupt</i> with messing with their decision to act, but you can't fine-tune your action either, just commit to the action you would do anyway.<br /> <br /> Or increase speed, the option you quoted and that is more powerful a speed burst, giving you movement equivalent to multiple actions, but is limited to your movement alone, hinting that you can do only so much so fast.<br /> <br /> My take also considers how broad and abstract I see the Defense stat, because it is the only property of the target that affects your own attack. Denying Defense makes the target effectively as vulnerable as a dummy or a box. So the question is: should this equate the target to a non-moving target? No reaction, no positioning, no difficulty whatsoever? Unless the answer is an unmistakable &quot;yes&quot;, I'm against denying Defense and even wary of penalizing it.<br /> <br /> But I do think other avenues may exist to explore the question. The Dodge roll certainly shouldn't be possible against such an attack, for example. And if you have a roll to feint or otherwise make an actually unexpected attack, then this roll could be benefited by the speed. A character that specifically hones their ability of exploring this blinding speed to penalize or ignore Defense through a Merit or Devotion would be a valid approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T09:18:56-08:00","id":1470787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470783#post1470783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take also considers how broad and abstract I see the Defense stat, because it is the only property of the target that affects your own attack. Denying Defense makes the target effectively as vulnerable as a dummy or a box. So the question is: should this equate the target to a non-moving target? No reaction, no positioning, no difficulty whatsoever? Unless the answer is an unmistakable &quot;yes&quot;, I'm against denying Defense and even wary of penalizing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is overstating things, because attacking a completely vulnerable target just uses the Killing Blow mechanics.<br /> <br /> Quoting from the newer iteration of the core mechanics used in 2e corebooks published after Promethean, &quot;Defense measures your character's ability to react to danger and mitigate harm to herself;&quot; the latter is the most probable explanation for why the Stalwart Numen changes what Attribute an ephemeral being uses to calculate Defense rather than giving it an Armor rating, or why the unnatural forms of a werewolf can still apply Defense against Firearms attacks (or, for that matter, why Celerity effectively gives a bonus to Defense that still applies against ranged attacks).<br /> <br /> If you <i>can</i> apply Defense to an attack, you choose whether or not to (such as if you want to avoid the cumulative penalty from multiple attackers and prioritize warding off a specific source of damage); the inability to apply Defense against ranged attacks is as much &quot;you can't really meaningfully roll with the punches of getting winged by a bullet&quot; as it is &quot;bullets move faster than most human reaction times.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Quoting further from that same iteration of the core mechanics, Surprise is sorted into the same part of the section on Action Scenes as Initiative, where it leads with talking about how surprise rolls might be called for &quot;if the start of an action might take a character unawares,&quot; with the examples provided being an ambush or being lulled into a false sense of security rather than simply vanishing for less than thirty seconds.<br /> <br /> The specific phrasing of not being able to act or apply Defense &quot;until their second turn&quot; is consistently used between both wordings of the mechanic, so I feel pretty confident that even in a fight where you can disappear at will you're not going to be automatically stopping your targets from ever taking a turn through the Surprise mechanics alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-18-2021, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T09:21:43-08:00","id":1470788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470783#post1470783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I just disagree that this speed equates to a penalty on Defense.<br /> <br /> Celerity has still a key limitation: you're still having only one action a turn. It gives you a burst of speed, but not an equal burst of <i>perception</i>. Your reaction time is, indeed, improved, but not by that much.<br /> <br /> It is the exact same situation of the bullet. Your target can't react properly, which is already covered by <i>Interrupt</i> with messing with their decision to act, but you can't fine-tune your action either, just commit to the action you would do anyway.<br /> <br /> Or increase speed, the option you quoted and that is more powerful a speed burst, giving you movement equivalent to multiple actions, but is limited to your movement alone, hinting that you can do only so much so fast.<br /> <br /> My take also considers how broad and abstract I see the Defense stat, because it is the only property of the target that affects your own attack. Denying Defense makes the target effectively as vulnerable as a dummy or a box. So the question is: should this equate the target to a non-moving target? No reaction, no positioning, no difficulty whatsoever? Unless the answer is an unmistakable &quot;yes&quot;, I'm against denying Defense and even wary of penalizing it.<br /> <br /> But I do think other avenues may exist to explore the question. The Dodge roll certainly shouldn't be possible against such an attack, for example. And if you have a roll to feint or otherwise make an actually unexpected attack, then this roll could be benefited by the speed. A character that specifically hones their ability of exploring this blinding speed to penalize or ignore Defense through a Merit or Devotion would be a valid approach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that at this point the problem is on the combat system itself, all of the issues you presented are all system related not the description of the discipline, my take is that the discipline of celerity isn't correctly represented in the game and in some ways, directly contradict its description but again, I still think that the whole system is to blame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T10:33:29-08:00","id":1470793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470787#post1470787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is overstating things, because attacking a completely vulnerable target just uses the Killing Blow mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is, it's a great exaggeration to compare a Defenseless target with a box. But otherwise my opinion stays the same. A character aware of a gunner definitely <b><i><u>can</u></i></b> meaningfully affect their attacker likelihood of hitting them even without cover. If this is by much or not, that's another issue, but a target moving regardless of you isn't as hard to hit as a target moving with self defense in mind.<br /> <br /> But then, this is already the rule, I can disagree or houserule it, not argue it isn't the rule. My point, though, is that I don't see a need to change Celerity as is. Getting this benefit mid-combat doesn't seems relevant. Moving four times your normal speed then interrupting is already plenty of benefit for an ambush, as you can almost guarantee your attack will come as a surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T12:08:39-08:00","id":1470797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470781#post1470781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it might not be a bullet but its definitely not something that you can easily predict and fight against, especially if you suddenly shift behind an opponent,</div> </div> </div> </div>No actually, a typical assumption in combat is that your opponent is going to actively attempt to move to your side or behind you, so they can hit you but you can't see them or hit back as hard. It's why martial arts have lots of techniques like the back kick, spin heel kick, reverse elbow, and shoulder throws, based on the premise you may not be squared off face to face with your attacker.<br /> Furthermore, practitioners learn to perform these techniques as instantaneous reactions, seeing the attacker isn't automatically required in order to perform them effectively.<br /> <br /> If a character has a single rank in Brawl, they are likely to know at least one tactic on how to react to getting hit from behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 12-18-2021, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T12:22:29-08:00","id":1470799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470797#post1470797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No actually, a typical assumption in combat is that your opponent is going to actively attempt to move to your side or behind you, so they can hit you but you can't see them or hit back as hard. It's why martial arts have lots of techniques like the back kick, spin heel kick, reverse elbow, and shoulder throws, based on the premise you may not be squared off face to face with your attacker.<br /> Furthermore, practitioners learn to perform these techniques as instantaneous reactions, seeing the attacker isn't automatically required in order to perform them effectively.<br /> <br /> If a character has a single rank in Brawl, they are likely to know at least one tactic on how to react to getting hit from behind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Come one man, a couple of mma classes aren't going to turn you into a monster killing machine, the first dot of celerity alone makes you faster beyond human capability, your reflexes simply aren't going to be able to counter something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T16:19:38-08:00","id":1470810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470797#post1470797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character has a single rank in Brawl, they are likely to know at least one tactic on how to react to getting hit from behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even that is needed. Being wary of unseen attacks is basic for anyone in a fight, and enough to provide some level of reaction, which is what your Defense rating represents.<br /> <br /> But yes, making and reacting to unseen threats is Combat 101, so being able to predict the attack isn't that big a factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470799#post1470799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come one man, a couple of mma classes aren't going to turn you into a monster killing machine, the first dot of celerity alone makes you faster beyond human capability, your reflexes simply aren't going to be able to counter something like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're not going to stop the monster from interrupting your actions or running really fast, two amazing feats of speed.<br /> <br /> But Celerity just isn't fine-tuned enough to grant any direct combat bonus. And I don't see the need for it to be.<br /> <br /> We are ultimately talking about a fantastic situation being modeled by a simplistic system. It is bound to be unable to actually represent all the minutiae of real combat. An opponent aware of you is already far from defenseless, no matter how much your blinding speed can give you an edge. If this edge is already covered by interrupting, why do you have such a need for ignoring Defense?<br /> <br /> I would be more moved by a balance argument for the Discipline than a realism argument for doing stuff faster than your own mind can actually process your movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T18:06:56-08:00","id":1470814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470810#post1470810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even that is needed. Being wary of unseen attacks is basic for anyone in a fight, and enough to provide some level of reaction, which is what your Defense rating represents.<br /> <br /> But yes, making and reacting to unseen threats is Combat 101, so being able to predict the attack isn't that big a factor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, they're not going to stop the monster from interrupting your actions or running really fast, two amazing feats of speed.<br /> <br /> But Celerity just isn't fine-tuned enough to grant any direct combat bonus. And I don't see the need for it to be.<br /> <br /> We are ultimately talking about a fantastic situation being modeled by a simplistic system. It is bound to be unable to actually represent all the minutiae of real combat. An opponent aware of you is already far from defenseless, no matter how much your blinding speed can give you an edge. If this edge is already covered by interrupting, why do you have such a need for ignoring Defense?<br /> <br /> I would be more moved by a balance argument for the Discipline than a realism argument for doing stuff faster than your own mind can actually process your movement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that the level of reaction should be greatly penalized by the fact that your opponent is basically teleporting all around you and that there is basically no way you could have the reaction time to do something about it, I mean we are talking about monsters here, being wary of attacks and having a black belt shouldn't save you from a bloodsucking monster with superhuman strength and speed.<br /> <br /> Like I wrote before, I think that the problem is with the system itself that simply doesn't really account for the, quite frankly, ridiculous ammount of power vampires have (or should have, based on what is written on the manual), I always wondered why the supposedly 2nd most physical splat after werewolves, feels like playing a human with some quirks and the inability to stand sun, at least untill you start dropping xp into it, I mean I have been in a game where 2 humans with baseball bats were able to drive off a daeva with both celerity and vigour, regardless of skill, this shouldn't be possible much like is not possible for a werewolf in gauru to be driven away by two assholes with baseball bat even if the werewolf in question doesn't have combat skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T21:05:23-08:00","id":1470817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470814#post1470814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean we are talking about monsters here, being wary of attacks and having a black belt shouldn't save you from a bloodsucking monster with superhuman strength and speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Superhuman strength is a separate power from Celerity, and the way melee attacks work mean that's the one that gives you more ability to overcome Defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I wrote before, I think that the problem is with the system itself that simply doesn't really account for the, quite frankly, ridiculous ammount of power vampires have (or should have, based on what is written on the manual), I always wondered why the supposedly 2nd most physical splat after werewolves, feels like playing a human with some quirks and the inability to stand sun, at least untill you start dropping xp into it, </div> </div> </div>Probably because the game is literally set up so that that's how you start \u2014 you don't pick up a Clan Bane until you drop below starting Humanity, and frenzy doesn't offer much of a bonus at BP one, and while the special experience type solely for raising Blood Potency is technically an optional rule (outside of diablerie), it <i>is</i> in the corebook for a reason.<br /> <br /> Like, the &quot;ridiculous amount of power&quot; vampires have out of the box is that they treat attacks from mortal weapons as though they were (maybe especially hefty) barehanded attacks, don't die when &quot;killed&quot; unless they were basically reduced to paste, can see in the dark, can trivially apply about five different exploitable Conditions to mortals for free, and can grab and bite for lethal damage as a single action when sufficiently incensed. In a system where combat is designed to chew through the Willpower of non-specialists and you can end a combat scene that isn't a fight to the death by dealing less than half a character's Health in bashing damage, that's a lot; much like Deviants, vampires are mostly dealing with mortals and each other.<br /> <br /> There's a character in JoJo's Bizarre Adventure who comes out the worse off in almost every straight fight he's involved in compared with the punchier abilities of the protagonist; this makes perfect sense, because that character is <i>a serial killer</i> with powers invisible to mortal eyes. Vampires aren't fighters unless they build to be, and their most generally-applicable free tool for getting around that requires putting time and/or effort into being a vampire that can survive as a vampire for decades at a time.<br /> <br /> The common refrain for Forsaken translates well enough to Requiem: much as the Uratha are hunters, not warriors, the Kindred are serial killers, not prizefighters. Their signature move is coming up behind someone in an alley or luring someone into the back rooms or sneaking into a sleeping person's bedroom, because their main application of violence is <i>to eat</i>, an act that in nature is fraught with vulnerability to such a degree that most things that aren't opportunistic scavengers or apex predators do it either in a secure location or with backup around if they can help it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean I have been in a game where 2 humans with baseball bats were able to drive off a daeva with both celerity and vigour, regardless of skill, this shouldn't be possible much like is not possible for a werewolf in gauru to be driven away by two assholes with baseball bat even if the werewolf in question doesn't have combat skills. </div> </div> </div>Gauru is the killing form for shapeshifting berserker demigods made to hunt down things that don't die easily at all. Vampires are territorial predators that adapt to suit their environment if they intend to survive; Vigor and Celerity notably give a character extra options for <i>getting out of the area</i>. Your Daeva was outnumbered and evidently didn't make use of the fact that the Predatory Aura is free to use against mortals to better scare them off or frenzy to Just Fucking Eat Them, but without concrete numbers I have no idea why you think Celerity and Vigor would outweigh skill in combat in a system that, again, is designed to make combat an especially bad approach for characters who aren't good at combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T01:16:30-08:00","id":1470828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470814#post1470814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I have been in a game where 2 humans with baseball bats were able to drive off a daeva with both celerity and vigour, regardless of skill, this shouldn't be possible much like is not possible for a werewolf in gauru to be driven away by two assholes with baseball bat even if the werewolf in question doesn't have combat skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have hard time to see how two normal guy with baseball bat can have beaten down a vampire, any vampire, at all.<br /> <br /> In all my games I really struggling to put any kind of pressure on my PC from Mortals. To not give them the feeling they can just step in everywhere without risks. Sometimes automatic guns/small rifles with quite a few number of enemy can work, otherwise it's always an easy game for the PC.<br /> <br /> In example: a normal thug with strg 3 weaponary/brawl 3 (which is even above the average for mortal standards) has a dicepool of 6. A Davea with Celerity may have easily defense of 5 6 reducing the dicepool of one of the thug to chance dice and to 1 die the second one. Which means, even in the fortunate case they make 1 success each with 1 die its 3 bashing damage each, 6 in total.<br /> <br /> Now, in the case your Daeva has only BP 1 it means that can either: heal up instantly 2 damages with a total of 4 bashing damage. But this would be the worst choice for a Davea who can only spend 1 vitae per turn. I would rather use interrupt to grapple with one of the thug, having a statistical edge to win the grapple (I'm not even considering frenzy to be able to bite same turn). In a grapple you control you are only worried by one of the thug still being able to apply your full defense against him (chance dice). You can bite and heal up at will leaving one of the opponent fainted to focus on the last one.<br /> <br /> If this strategy doesn't work at the very first turn, they still have to be able to hit you several turn in order to be able to send you in torpor. 4 bashing per turn (considering the healing - as you can only use interrupt once per scene considering Celerity only 1) means that, for an average Daeva with 7 health points they have to bypass (and you have to lose the grapple) 4 consecutive turns before to have you in torpor. Before that I presume you would go in Frenzy.<br /> <br /> And I'm only considering a BP 1 Vigor 1 Celerity 1 vampire and only accounting physical means leaving out all the other, and most efficient, ways to deal with mortal (Majesty, scaring the shit out of them etc. Also Celerity and Vigor would have allowed the Daeva to easily run away in the very unlikely situation to lose 4 turns against a chance dice pool. May be the Daeva was inexpert and didn't played properly his cards?<br /> <br /> Also, talking about raw physical numbers, Vampire splat grow even more dangerous of a werewolf at BP above 5-6. And the higher the BP the most dangerous the vampire. The real advantage a werewolf has is Killer Instinct, which is a level 1 power that allow to acquire the 8's again on brawl rolls. Which is nothing impossible to cover with a very simple devotion though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T03:25:20-08:00","id":1470837,"title":"","content":"&quot;I think that the level of reaction should be greatly penalized by the fact that your opponent is basically teleporting all around you and that there is basically no way you could have the reaction time to do something about it&quot;<br /> <br /> Except 1. They're not teleporting. They ARE physically crossing that space and they ARE visible. Vampires don't move faster than the speed of sound much less light, so they can be perceived. (Not only that, humans visually detect motion in their peripheral vision ranges better than straightforward changes in the light.) Then there's the fact that the brain processes and interprets partial sensory clues to fill in what it discerns even before it obtains all of the details. So that superspeed doesn't make vampires nearly as undetectable and therefore others as defenseless as you wish it did. 2. They are not taking a reaction, their defensive maneuver is done in anticipation that celerity asshole is going to (in utter predictable and unimaginative fashion) close the distance and path to their victim's left or right side in an attempt to get behind them. The moment a victim with some practical melee experience sees the asshole with celerity, they shift to a defensive side stance and do something like swing their left foot in a into a low sweeping arc. After celerity asshole predictably rushes forward and punches their victim in the face, the celerity asshole's ankle connects with the left foot of their victim's sweeping kick. Following through on the direction of their arc kick, combined with celerity asshole's own speed, he faceplants straight into the ground at whatever super enhanced speed he was moving. After all celerity does not grant enhanced combat skill by itself. You have to apply the tertiary uses for effective combat use.<br /> And seriously, if a 1 BP Daeva gets their ass handed to him by two human clowns with baseball bats, the humans would be doing kindred society a favor removing him from the kindred gene pool. He could have used Celerity to interrupt the first attack, snatching the bat from his attacker and avoiding the other's strike by moving out of range. Next turn moving back in range and repeating the interrupt process. At which point the two bat clowns either flee or resort to other weapons and the Daeva uses vigor to beat them senseless with their own bats.<br /> <br /> Of course if said Daeva bothered using Predatory Aura or using a rank of Majesty, (yeah those lame non combat powers) he could intimidate them into fleeing or seduce them into working alongside him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 12-19-2021, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T05:34:19-08:00","id":1470840,"title":"","content":"I should elaborate on the Daeva example, said vampire had 1 dots in strength, 2 dots from vigour and 1 in brawl so while definitely not a powerhouse she was definitely combat capable, now, the two thugs were your average run of the mill thugs with baseball bats, don't exactly remember all their stats but I think it was at least strength 3 and brawl 2, now she first tried to lash out with the seductive beast since she had 4 dots of presence and 1 bp, plus 3 from willpower for a total of 8 dices and she failed the roll, so she went on the offensive rolling 4 dices plus 3 from willpower (she spent a vitae for the weapon modifier from vigour) minus 4 from the thug defence, she again fails the roll, meanwhile the first thug rolls 5 minus 3 (the daeva had 3 dots in dexterity and one celerity but she lacked athletics so minus 1) and hits with 2 successes plus 2 from the bat for a total of 4 bashing, the second thug has the same dices but rolls with minus 2 because of the reduced defense from the first attack and scores 3 successes plus 2 from the bat for a grand total of 9 bashing damage that rolled over to 2 lethal, the daeva at this point, figuring that this wasn't her night, use celerity to get away.<br /> <br /> You might think that the above example could be chalked to really bad luck but the fact remain that 2 assholes with baseball bats managed to drive off an immortal superpredator, I understand that the combat system is designed to give more of a fighting chance to mortals compared to oWoD but come on.<br /> <br /> I personally think that celerity, along with the other physical disciplines, should receive a nice makeover to give them more of an edge against mortals rather than just a couple of extra dices, this might be because I am mainly a werewolf player and I'm used to consider humans a non factor when it comes to combat but I find the idea of a vampire getting their ass handed to them like this really underwhelming, I have played quite a few vampire games but since I focus on stealthy characters and avoid combat whennever possible, I had never realized how weak they are in the beginning unless they are specifically built for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T05:40:21-08:00","id":1470841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470837#post1470837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I think that the level of reaction should be greatly penalized by the fact that your opponent is basically teleporting all around you and that there is basically no way you could have the reaction time to do something about it&quot;<br /> <br /> Except 1. They're not teleporting. They ARE physically crossing that space and they ARE visible. Vampires don't move faster than the speed of sound much less light, so they can be perceived. (Not only that, humans visually detect motion in their peripheral vision ranges better than straightforward changes in the light.) Then there's the fact that the brain processes and interprets partial sensory clues to fill in what it discerns even before it obtains all of the details. So that superspeed doesn't make vampires nearly as undetectable and therefore others as defenseless as you wish it did. 2. They are not taking a reaction, their defensive maneuver is done in anticipation that celerity asshole is going to (in utter predictable and unimaginative fashion) close the distance and path to their victim's left or right side in an attempt to get behind them. The moment a victim with some practical melee experience sees the asshole with celerity, they shift to a defensive side stance and do something like swing their left foot in a into a low sweeping arc. After celerity asshole predictably rushes forward and punches their victim in the face, the celerity asshole's ankle connects with the left foot of their victim's sweeping kick. Following through on the direction of their arc kick, combined with celerity asshole's own speed, he faceplants straight into the ground at whatever super enhanced speed he was moving. After all celerity does not grant enhanced combat skill by itself. You have to apply the tertiary uses for effective combat use.<br /> And seriously, if a 1 BP Daeva gets their ass handed to him by two human clowns with baseball bats, the humans would be doing kindred society a favor removing him from the kindred gene pool. He could have used Celerity to interrupt the first attack, snatching the bat from his attacker and avoiding the other's strike by moving out of range. Next turn moving back in range and repeating the interrupt process. At which point the two bat clowns either flee or resort to other weapons and the Daeva uses vigor to beat them senseless with their own bats.<br /> <br /> Of course if said Daeva bothered using Predatory Aura or using a rank of Majesty, (yeah those lame non combat powers) he could intimidate them into fleeing or seduce them into working alongside him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Multiply her speed by her dots in Celerity plus one. Moving in this way is sudden, jarring, the vampire appears to shift from point to point without crossing the space in-between&quot; straight out of the manual, so yeah, they are not visible and the karate kid in question should find himself with his throat ripped out before he could process what was happening let alone use all the 40 hours or so of self defense classes he had at this point to try emulate Chuck Norris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T05:45:09-08:00","id":1470842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470840#post1470840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should elaborate on the Daeva example, said vampire had 1 dots in strength, 2 dots from vigour and 1 in brawl so while definitely not a powerhouse she was definitely combat capable, now, the two thugs were your average run of the mill thugs with baseball bats, don't exactly remember all their stats but I think it was at least strength 3 and brawl 2, now she first tried to lash out with the seductive beast since she had 4 dots of presence and 1 bp, plus 3 from willpower for a total of 8 dices and she failed the roll, so she went on the offensive rolling 4 dices plus 3 from willpower (she spent a vitae for the weapon modifier from vigour) minus 4 from the thug defence, she again fails the roll, meanwhile the first thug rolls 5 minus 3 (the daeva had 3 dots in dexterity and one celerity but she lacked athletics so minus 1) and hits with 2 successes plus 2 from the bat for a total of 4 bashing, the second thug has the same dices but rolls with minus 2 because of the reduced defense from the first attack and scores 3 successes plus 2 from the bat for a grand total of 9 bashing damage that rolled over to 2 lethal, the daeva at this point, figuring that this wasn't her night, use celerity to get away.<br /> <br /> You might think that the above example could be chalked to really bad luck but the fact remain that 2 assholes with baseball bats managed to drive off an immortal superpredator, I understand that the combat system is designed to give more of a fighting chance to mortals compared to oWoD but come on.<br /> <br /> I personally think that celerity, along with the other physical disciplines, should receive a nice makeover to give them more of an edge against mortals rather than just a couple of extra dices, this might be because I am mainly a werewolf player and I'm used to consider humans a non factor when it comes to combat but I find the idea of a vampire getting their ass handed to them like this really underwhelming, I have played quite a few vampire games but since I focus on stealthy characters and avoid combat whennever possible, I had never realized how weak they are in the beginning unless they are specifically built for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honstly, stregth 1 and Brawl 1 seems to me a below normality human being, no matter Vigor which brought him up to a total of strength 3. It's a bit of a badly built character if you invest 2 dots in vigor having strength 1. Non the less I believe there are some mistake:<br /> <br /> 1. You do not activate Vigor before rolling the dice. You roll your pool, then, if you hit, you reflexively activate Vigor to add automatic damages. So he could have 1 vitae to spend after he failed the roll.<br /> 2. Why not having athletic lower your defense? I might be wrong but the penalty of not having a skill only apply when rolling that skill. Defense is built on lower between dex/wits + athl+ celerity.<br /> <br /> Also, being unlucky with rolling dice it's part of a game which use dice. But, statistically, he still have the edge on the combat. <br /> I still think he could have easily won using celerity to interrupt the firts or second hit even just moving away, completely avoid 5 damages or simply passing first in initiative in the following rounds. Also going for grapple would have taken away one of the thug for the remaining turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T06:00:13-08:00","id":1470843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470842#post1470842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honstly, stregth 1 and Brawl 1 seems to me a below normality human being, no matter Vigor which brought him up to a total of strength 3. It's a bit of a badly built character if you invest 2 dots in vigor having strength 1. Non the less I believe there are some mistake:<br /> <br /> 1. You do not activate Vigor before rolling the dice. You roll your pool, then, if you hit, you reflexively activate Vigor to add automatic damages. So he could have 1 vitae to spend after he failed the roll.<br /> 2. Why not having athletic lower your defense? I might be wrong but the penalty of not having a skill only apply when rolling that skill. Defense is built on lower between dex/wits + athl+ celerity.<br /> <br /> Also, being unlucky with rolling dice it's part of a game which use dice. But, statistically, he still have the edge on the combat.<br /> I still think he could have easily won using celerity to interrupt the firts or second hit even just moving away, completely avoid 5 damages or simply passing first in initiative in the following rounds. Also going for grapple would have taken away one of the thug for the remaining turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The character was more of a talker than a fighter and really took vigor and celerity to substitute her lack of combat skills (wasn't my character btw), I don't think you can just activate vigor before hitting, that would be like activating resilience after the damage was done, regarding athletic from my understanding, you subtract the penalty everytime the skills apply so even when calculating defense.<br /> <br /> The daeva took a lot of damage from the first round alone and she was only bp 1 so she could have either healed or use a discipline, she also only had 3 more willpower dots left and didn't want to waste them so she opted to run, grappling wouldn't have resolved much since her combat pool was still a chance die even with willpower (she had minus 3 from the full track of bashing she had).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-19-2021, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T06:08:44-08:00","id":1470844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470843#post1470843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The character was more of a talker than a fighter and really took vigor and celerity to substitute her lack of combat skills (wasn't my character btw), I don't think you can just activate vigor before hitting, that would be like activating resilience after the damage was done, regarding athletic from my understanding, you subtract the penalty everytime the skills apply so even when calculating defense.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can. Same for Resilience. Activating physical's discipline is reflexive as healing up. You can do it anytime in the turn. You hit, then you activate vigor.<br /> Same way you get damaged, then you can use resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T06:43:35-08:00","id":1470847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470844#post1470844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can. Same for Resilience. Activating physical's discipline is reflexive as healing up. You can do it anytime in the turn. You hit, then you activate vigor.<br /> Same way you get damaged, then you can use resilience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems a bit like cheating to be honest, I'm unsure about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T07:20:31-08:00","id":1470851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470847#post1470847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems a bit like cheating to be honest, I'm unsure about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The active effects are reflexive, which means you can (and should) activate them as a response. No need to activate them preemptively. That kind of gambling with resources (that are limited in both amount and has spending limits) is generally not satisfying game design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T07:43:00-08:00","id":1470852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470851#post1470851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The active effects are reflexive, which means you can (and should) activate them as a response. No need to activate them preemptively. That kind of gambling with resources (that are limited in both amount and has spending limits) is generally not satisfying game design.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way I interpret it is that once the attack connects, you shouldn't be able to mitigate or enhance damage since its already done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T08:26:48-08:00","id":1470856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470817#post1470817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>to eat</i>, an act that in nature is fraught with vulnerability to such a degree that most things that aren't opportunistic scavengers or apex predators do it either in a secure location or with backup around if they can help it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: even apex predators do it at a safe location or with backup. Very few eat on the site of the kill if they don't have security measures in place, not even tigers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470840#post1470840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the two thugs were your average run of the mill thugs with baseball bats, don't exactly remember all their stats but I think it was at least strength 3 and brawl 2 ... 4 from the thug defence</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to what other said, this is not a run-of-the-mill thug, this is a clearly above average combatant. Facing a complete non-combatant relying on a few supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> On the skill penalty: Defense isn't a use of the skill, it is its own stat. The fact the skill is applied in its calculation doesn't change that Defense is a separate stat and won't be affected by penalties that are not specific for it.<br /> <br /> Your expectations on the supernatural benefits granting direct combat prowess are off with the game intents, the same for how Celerity works. The game isn't intended to make personal skill be absolutely inferior to early supernatural prowess, period. A skilled fighter hardly is life-threatening by themselves, but must be taken into account, because Vampire is more modular in your preternatural leanings than Werewolf (where almost everything makes you a better combatant early on).<br /> <br /> The Celerity user isn't seemingly teleporting all around. They're seemingly teleporting sometimes. At best twice a round, and even then one of those is more like a sudden burst of movement than a teleport, as interrupting does not implies change of location, just sudden action. And it clearly doesn't imply the vampire's perception and reaction accompanies fully this burst of speed, so even while a vampire can use it to &quot;teleport&quot; to your back, they'll need a more human-like time to take stock of things before acting properly on it, hence they not getting any bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470852#post1470852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I interpret it is that once the attack connects, you shouldn't be able to mitigate or enhance damage since its already done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet this is not the rule, but think about it that way: this is not about making a decision or activating a power from a character perspective, but about the Discipline not wasting Blood. You can either think that the Disciplines are active before but do not consume Vitae when the effect is negligible (like striking air), or you can interpret that they're activating in a mystic non-time since they <b>are</b> preternatural abilities.<br /> <br /> One way or another, the point is that consume blood beforehand will cause them to be less useful and harder to manage, so it is not the best option to have your game running smoothly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T09:54:03-08:00","id":1470862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-attacks?p=1470852#post1470852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The way I interpret it is that once the attack connects, you shouldn't be able to mitigate or enhance damage since its already done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Reflexive means you can activate anytime. It is designed to be used after the attack hit and I believe it works just fine like that. Otherwise you should always chose in advance what you want to activate risking to waste precious vitae for nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T18:07:05-08:00","id":1471061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1470706-celerity-and-surprise-